WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.600 --> 00:00:01.936
Hello, I'm Camille.

2
00:00:02.286 --> 00:00:04.806
Today: when the scam arrives by post.

3
00:00:05.506 --> 00:00:09.826
You receive a letter with your bank's logo. It looks very official.

4
00:00:10.176 --> 00:00:15.448
You're asked to scan a QR code, to reactivate your card, or secure your account.

5
00:00:15.798 --> 00:00:18.446
A deadline pushes you to act fast.

6
00:00:18.796 --> 00:00:23.476
The QR code leads to a fake website that imitates your bank's, and steals your login details.

7
00:00:24.176 --> 00:00:26.520
The same trap exists in the street.

8
00:00:26.870 --> 00:00:32.206
Fake QR codes are sometimes stuck on parking meters, to make you pay on a fake website.

9
00:00:32.906 --> 00:00:34.434
The right reflexes.

10
00:00:34.784 --> 00:00:38.232
For a letter, call your branch on the number you already know.

11
00:00:38.582 --> 00:00:42.830
After scanning, always check the website address before typing anything.

12
00:00:43.180 --> 00:00:46.676
And be wary of QR codes stuck over another one, or damaged.

13
00:00:47.376 --> 00:00:49.368
Distrust is the mother of safety.

14
00:00:49.718 --> 00:00:52.502
That was Camille, for Prometis. See you soon!
